To incorporate the STOR and TYPE commands into the sequence of client requests, we need to consider the context in which these commands are typically used. The TYPE command is usually issued after the user logs in and before any data transfer commands like STOR or RETR. The STOR command is used to upload a file to the server.

Here’s the modified sequence with STOR and TYPE added in appropriate locations:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
TYPE I       ; Set the transfer type to binary (I for Image)
STOR filename.txt  ; Upload a file named filename.txt
LIST
MKD test
QUIT
```

In this sequence:
- The TYPE command is added after the PORT command to set the transfer mode before any file transfer commands.
- The STOR command is added right after the TYPE command to upload a file named `filename.txt`. You can replace `filename.txt` with the actual name of the file you want to upload.

If you have a specific file name or type in mind, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly!

